(7452237, 1179735, 6519, '<td valign="top">I was not impressed by this very blurry, noisy, unrecognizable blob, but I was willing to be convinced into an apology in case I was at fault of missing something amazing.<br/> <br/>After roll-over, I checked this image.<br/> <br/>Still no explanation, absolutely NO notes, no explanations, no details, in fact there is nothing whatsoever. <br/> <br/>I am now happy I voted a 2.<br/> <br/>However, you are a new member. Should you enjoy a little bit of help and some pointers, please send me a message and I''ll do my best.</td>', 'I was not impressed by this very blurry, noisy, unrecognizable blob, but I was willing to be convinced into an apology in case I was at fault of missing something amazing. After roll-over, I checked this image. Still no explanation, absolutely NO notes, no explanations, no details, in fact there is nothing whatsoever.  I am now happy I voted a 2. However, you are a new member. Should you enjoy a little bit of help and some pointers, please send me a message and I''ll do my best.', '2016-04-27 06:20:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7452238, 1179665, 6519, '<td valign="top">Aaaawww...... I was one of your 8''s. This screams "junque" at me. <br/> <br/>Never mind...... cute shot.</td>', 'Aaaawww...... I was one of your 8''s. This screams "junque" at me.  Never mind...... cute shot.', '2016-04-27 06:22:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7452239, 1179737, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge well.<br/> <br/>As Aimee says, what a great find. These sort of places are an endless source of fascination, anticipation and surprise. I like the creative way you have approached the subject by introducing a deliberate angle but a crop would improve it. The telegraph pole on the right is superfluous and distracting and we dont really need any sky above. A crop that includes the 140 sign at the bottom right but excludes the pole, you would need to clone out the two power lines from it, and removing the top to just below the weatherboard, in my mind, improves the end result. If you do that I would also clone out the two spotlights at the top of the frame or else they would then become distracting, you could also ease the detail out in the foreground with a little dodging.<br/> <br/>Thanks for an interesting entry Camelia</td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge well. As Aimee says, what a great find. These sort of places are an endless source of fascination, anticipation and surprise. I like the creative way you have approached the subject by introducing a deliberate angle but a crop would improve it. The telegraph pole on the right is superfluous and distracting and we dont really need any sky above. A crop that includes the 140 sign at the bottom right but excludes the pole, you would need to clone out the two power lines from it, and removing the top to just below the weatherboard, in my mind, improves the end result. If you do that I would also clone out the two spotlights at the top of the frame or else they would then become distracting, you could also ease the detail out in the foreground with a little dodging. Thanks for an interesting entry Camelia', '2016-04-27 06:35:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(7452241, 1179479, 6519, '<td valign="top">I was so hoping you''d enlighten us about what on earth you were showing us, or trying to express.<br/> <br/>Alas........... NO notes, explanations.......... still no clue!!!!<br/> <br/>Come on........ this "image" really needs some guidance!!!!</td>', 'I was so hoping you''d enlighten us about what on earth you were showing us, or trying to express. Alas........... NO notes, explanations.......... still no clue!!!! Come on........ this "image" really needs some guidance!!!!', '2016-04-27 06:39:57.000000', NULL, 0),
